  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **An endpoint's process lock is a file beside the database file, held open, instead of a system mutex,** Compze.Threading.Interprocess's `IProcessLock`. Every process that can open the database reaches it, whichever user it runs as, where the mutex was per machine; the operating system still releases it when its process dies. An in-memory database's lock is in `Compze/EndpointProcessLocks` in the temp directory, as is a `file:` URI data source's. Holding it no longer parks a thread for each endpoint: only the thread that took a mutex could release it.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.Threading.Interprocess 0.8.0-alpha (was 0.7.1-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
